    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26886" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏcātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		loco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who lets, a letter, hirer out</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					19, 2, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insulae et fundi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
				35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
				36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meretricum, Firm. Math. 4, 6: LOCATOR A SCENA
					or SCENICORVM,</span>”
				<i>one who furnished for a stipulated sum the actors and
						stage apparatus to him who gave a play</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2618 sq.</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2629</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A contractor, undertaker</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">funeris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 52, 53, § 176</span></i>
			.</div>
